cing  old furnaces  our chief political correspondent david  aiken explains the theory behind it  and how to apply well donna back in 2007  the harper government had a very similar  home energy retrofit program and it was  wildly popular more than  half a million canadians took federal  cash for  home renovations before that program was  shut down in 2012.  but now the trudeau government is  resurrecting that program  turning what the harper government  called the eco energy retrofit program  into the canada greener homes grant  program  a cash handout of up to five thousand  dollars to homeowners  for qualifying projects as a homeowner  you don't want to have to pay extra  money on energy bills because of a leaky  window  when you could save that money for  school supplies or groceries  and as a country every effort counts to  keep our air clean and our environment  healthy eligible projects could include  replacing oil furnaces or low efficiency  systems  improving or replacing insulation  installing  high efficiency water heaters or solar  panels  fixing drafty windows or doors this is  a good program to fight climate change  save homeowners money  and uh and create jobs but there are  many other things we're doing as well  minutes after trudeau's announcement an  online portal opened up  where homeowners can apply to get into  the program i was going to make our  business go through the roof there's no  doubt about it in fact  as i was just mentioning to you my  phone's been ringing off the hook for  the last two hours  people hearing about the news the grants  are also retroactive  for work done as far back as december  1st 2020  but there's no hurry the program is set  to run  for the next five years and it might be  a while before canadians can take full  advantage of this program  for one thing with the home building  boom in many cities around the country  it can be tough to find a contractor in  second with the price of lumber and  other building materials near an  all-time  high well doing a home rental right now  might be kind of pricey even with  the federal cash donna  all right david aiken in ottawa thanks  still ahead china fights back on  theories about the origins of covid19  china is accusing the biden  administration of politicizing the  investigation into the origins of the  novel coronavirus  president biden has ordered a review of  the intelligence about  where the virus emerged a chinese  foreign ministry spokesperson says this  shows that  they don't care about the facts or the  truth and have zero interest in a  serious science-based study of origins  their one aim is to use the pandemic to  pursue stigmatization and political  manipulation to shift the blame  the theory that the virus may have  accidentally leaked from a lab in wuhan  in late 2019  is gaining traction china has repeatedly  denied any link  prime minister justin trudeau says he  supports the call by the u.s and other  countries to better understand the  origins of covet 19 to  ensure accountability and better protect  the world  from future pandemics  next an apology decades after the  internment of italian canadians  what we owe each other is the truth that  was the message from french president  emmanuel macron  rwanda today he asked for forgiveness  and admitted france bears terrible  responsibility for the 1994 rwandan  genocide  mackerel said well france was not an  accomplice in the genocide  terrible errors in judgment were made  and warnings ignored  he said france had for too long valued  silence over examination of the truth  ethnic hutus killed more than 800 000  people most of them  members of the tutsi minority in carnage  that lasted  about 100 days france and other western  powers  failed to intervene to the men  and women who were taken to prisoner of  war camps  or jail without charge  people who are no longer with us to hear  this apology  to the tens of thousands of innocent  italian canadians who were labeled  enemy aliens we  prime minister trudeau formally  apologized today to italian canadians  who were sent to internment camps during  the second world war  it was feared they were supporters of  the fascist italian dictator benito  mussolini who had allied himself with  adolf hitler  though as mike armstrong explains some  of those in turned had sons fighting  in the canadian military there is  very little left today but this site in  kananaskis alberta was once  internment camp 130. it's one of the  places where during the second world war  italian canadians were locked up none of  those men are still alive today but  their experiences are still felt  by the generations that followed  salvatore vestarki was picked up in june  of 1940  in montreal 33 months of his life wiped  off the slate  your father could have been bitter  no oh yeah he was could have been no he  wasn't  he wasn't he just wondered why  when italy allied itself with nazi  germany in 1940  canada declared about 31 000 italian  canadians  as enemy aliens about 600 men and four  women were interned  without a trial salvatore vistaki spent  most of his time  in this camp in petawawa ontario after  being picked up  on the day he asked his girlfriend to  marry him  that that's a real hurt to go home  after a nice dinner after finally  finding the girl or finding the man that  you want you go to bed you're happy and  there's a knock on your door  and the next thing you're in handcuffs  not too nice now for some there was  insult added to injury there were men  who were interned by canada  while their sons fought for canada in  europe there was even a man whose son  had to leave school to support the  family  and was then conscripted into the  canadian army  my father built both sides of the street  starchy's father  rebuilt his life and went into business  as a homebuilder  he basically built the whole  neighborhood his daughter says he would  always tell her  someday there would be justice  she says this was that day  it's a happy day how unfortunate  is it that this apology comes when your  father's not here to hear us yeah  yeah that's what i really regret at  least if  one of them had been alive that would  have been  amazing but you know what  they know they know  mike armstrong global news montreal  and that is global national for this  thursday i'm donna friesen  we leave you tonight with news about a  book that was in heavy rotation in my  house and the homes of millions of  people  the man who created the very hungry  caterpillar has died  eric carl was an author and illustrator  who created many other beloved classics  he was 91 years old his team posted on  twitter thank you for sharing your  talent with generations  of young readers take care of yourselves  [Music]  [Applause]  bye-bye
 

